%erg 0.1
Title: Spec does not say where a ticket path starts
Created: 2026-09-16
Author: claude

--- log ---
2026-09-16T11:06Z claude created

--- body ---
## Context

`spec-erg-v1.md` "Closed / not-closed criterion", case 1:

> **Path test.** A path component (directory name or basename without
> extension) equals `closed` (case-insensitive), starts with `closed-` or
> `closed.`, or ends with `-closed`.

It never says where the path *starts*. Ticket 0285 is what that omission cost:
the implementation tested every component it was handed, so a checkout sitting
under a directory named `*-closed` made `erg check` fail on every ticket in the
store -- but only when the store was addressed by an absolute path.

0285 settled the question in code: the tested path is the part below the
directory `erg` was given -- the components the store walk itself descended
through, the ticket's own option 2. That is a narrowing, not a reversal --
both examples the spec gives (`tickets/closed/`, `0001-foo-closed.erg`) are
already store-relative -- and `TestStorePath` now enforces it. But the normative
document served by `erg spec` still does not state it, so the rule is guarded
without being written down. A reimplementation from the spec alone would
reproduce the 0285 defect exactly.

This is the "guarded-without-statement" case FOUNDATIONS-PROCESS.md names, and
its trigger (a change to a contract surface) was met by 0285.

Deliberately NOT folded into 0285: that branch touches no `src/go/assets/`
file, and a sibling PR (0283, assets) was open across its whole life. An asset
edit also owes the dogfood regeneration, which is a second reason to land it
on its own.

## Relevant files

- `src/go/assets/spec-erg-v1.md` -- the spec, embedded in the binary and served
  by `erg spec`. It is the only copy: `make regen-assets` covers `.ergrc` and
  `AGENTS.md`, not this file, so nothing needs regenerating here.
- `src/go/erg.go` (`StorePath`) -- the behaviour to describe; its doc comment is
  the draft
- `tests/test_docs.sh:60` -- the sibling guard for ticket 0256 ("spec documents
  the basename-only closure violation erg check emits"), the pattern to copy

## Actions

1. Add one sentence to case 1 saying which path is tested: the one below the
   directory `erg` was given, never the directories at or above it.
2. Add the doc guard next to the 0256 one in `tests/test_docs.sh`.

## Test

Red step in `tests/test_docs.sh`, modelled on the existing 0256 guard: assert
the spec's closure-criterion section says where the path begins (e.g. a grep
for `store root` within that section). It must fail against today's spec before
the sentence is added -- run it first and watch it fail, since a grep that
matches somewhere else in the file would pass vacuously.

## Verification

- [ ] `tests/test_docs.sh` fails on the pre-sentence spec and passes after
- [ ] `erg spec` on the rebuilt binary shows the sentence -- the embedded copy
      is what users read, so checking the source file alone would not prove it
      shipped
- [ ] The diff touches only the spec and `tests/test_docs.sh`

## Invariants

- No behaviour change. This ticket only writes down what 0285 already enforces;
  if a sentence seems to require a code change, the sentence is wrong.
- `make check` stays green, selfcoherence included.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `spec-erg-v1.md` case 1 states where the tested path starts
- [ ] A doc guard fails without the sentence and passes with it
- [ ] `erg spec` on the rebuilt binary shows the sentence
- [ ] `make check` passes
